#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115059 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115229 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e970fe-cff8-50e3-9b94-67ad97b03da7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "f832e671-b4bd-5d1d-81e7-b215a8ee4e27" :question/math-academy-id "e-4414" :question/problem "Find $A^4$ given that ![](images/45/45b13bcb5bbd8dc54e605acf6d378f582dcb7a4f2ecfff35a7a5343ee30f0515.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, to find $A^2,$ we multiply $A$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $A^4 = A^2 \\cdot A^2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{4} & ={A}^{2}\\cdot {A}^{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}81 & 0 \\\\ 100 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115060 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61443225-bc08-5d36-a603-3a1d7e392a98" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial"}] :question/id #uuid "bea8819f-6feb-5de6-a585-4379378ccdbd" :question/math-academy-id "e-4417" :question/problem "Consider the matrix\n![](images/b0/b070684b11de0098cac091b9132ef6276679177fa6dce1a8129f7951f6013c8c.png)\nFind $f(D)$ if $f(X)=-X^2+3X+2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & =-{X}^{2}+3X+2 \\\\  & =-{X}^{2}+3X+2I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(D)=-D^2+3D+2I.$\n\nLet's calculate $D^2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{2} & =D\\cdot D \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(D)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(D) & =-{D}^{2}+3D+2I \\\\  & =-[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 & 15 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+3+2 & 10+15+0 \\\\ 0 & -9-9+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 25 \\\\ 0 & -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388111 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115229 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e970fe-cff8-50e3-9b94-67ad97b03da7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7404f17f-430a-52fc-ad31-5483dd3d422f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388113} {:answer/id #uuid "6f785005-ba15-55aa-b2c1-49679b83ded2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 24 \\\\ -24 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388114} {:answer/id #uuid "44f9cc8e-2832-5d4d-bde3-6190366eb16a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 24\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388115} {:answer/id #uuid "f019d3e6-60c1-5087-aea8-8fc0704643d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388116} {:answer/id #uuid "aa01cfa5-4d7f-5746-8b64-c7431f690793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f785005-ba15-55aa-b2c1-49679b83ded2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 24 \\\\ -24 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388114} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6c03279-962c-5d34-91c8-4ce634a93747" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a0990577-78da-5706-a148-fc38d54b37ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-130582" :question/problem "If $U=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]$, then ${U}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, to find ${U}^{2},$ we multiply $U$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{2} & =U\\cdot U \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${U}^{3}={U}^{2}\\cdot U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{3} & ={U}^{2}\\cdot U \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 24 \\\\ -24 & -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388146 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61443225-bc08-5d36-a603-3a1d7e392a98" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98d46de3-1964-521e-987f-3f87e63d14f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388148} {:answer/id #uuid "290eb367-b69e-51e9-b010-dd7d2e86e6ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388149} {:answer/id #uuid "8ec94462-c5a9-5b19-af43-e4fb15a1b17d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388150} {:answer/id #uuid "def69761-fa9a-5675-91a9-81ca5a36b65a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388151} {:answer/id #uuid "cdeec92a-fd20-575e-a12b-6d715aa8a4a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "290eb367-b69e-51e9-b010-dd7d2e86e6ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388149} :answer-field/id #uuid "56b6390d-ed7e-571e-81e8-62f931b08ef6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388147}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "22954632-a7ef-5551-8cda-37dd0def8e71" :question/math-academy-id "q-130688" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $K=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find $f(K)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}-4X+1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-4X+1 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-4X+I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(K)={K}^{2}-4K+I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${K}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{K}^{2} & =K\\cdot K \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(K):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(K) & ={K}^{2}-4K+I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 7\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 8\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7-8+1 & 4-4-0 \\\\ 12-12+0 & 7-8+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295080 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61443225-bc08-5d36-a603-3a1d7e392a98" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6034546-7d4e-5c51-9fd2-f41fcfef04a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6034546-7d4e-5c51-9fd2-f41fcfef04a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293585} :answer-field/id #uuid "1428d1b1-1543-5a2a-9556-2cee443c52dc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293995} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26a75419-4630-5608-bb8c-21f42f59fc89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26a75419-4630-5608-bb8c-21f42f59fc89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293101} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dd27018-7e5e-55e0-a7db-154856c32454" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294202} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f82b6ae6-019e-5945-bcdb-f89f1c5c18ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f82b6ae6-019e-5945-bcdb-f89f1c5c18ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293903} :answer-field/id #uuid "9abe320a-1cfe-5902-8ad6-e836ba61c767" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294485} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f8b3b10-e90c-5a95-9564-16ee1de78c43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f8b3b10-e90c-5a95-9564-16ee1de78c43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293447} :answer-field/id #uuid "be6cf5de-bb45-5c30-9c0b-1503c34cb2b5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294607}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c36b6f56-91db-51b0-af6f-adc2bb76fc3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-279493" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ If $f(X)={X}^{2}+1$, find $f(A).$\n\n| $f(A)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}+1 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}+I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(A)={A}^{2}+I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${A}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & ={A}^{2}+I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+1 & 0+0 \\\\ 0+0 & -1+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365538 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61443225-bc08-5d36-a603-3a1d7e392a98" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b2de13f-7428-5cf4-a15d-bb759547b2ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b2de13f-7428-5cf4-a15d-bb759547b2ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365540} :answer-field/id #uuid "11f8211f-fddf-5d62-b133-32198e03aa6f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365539} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ea4d763-c8fb-5f15-8550-82d38c91fb41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ea4d763-c8fb-5f15-8550-82d38c91fb41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365542} :answer-field/id #uuid "442f54fb-8ea0-51fb-bfe8